title the position words both parsers refuse

# Kept out of the byte-exact cross-parser diff because the two
# parsers word this refusal differently, not because they disagree
# about it. treecheck.sh asserts both refusals, so "they differ only
# in wording" is a checked claim rather than a remembered one.
#
# These names are refused because they carry NO DIRECTION, not
# because they carry the wrong one. The reference parser used to
# accept them as aliases, and it is tempting to record that the
# aliases were backwards -- but two people who had both read this
# project closely turned out to hold opposite mappings, and each
# found the same fixture plausible. There was never a correct
# direction to preserve.
#
# That is exactly how a mirrored fixture survives review, and it is
# the argument for deleting the words rather than fixing them. The
# roles are onto and off-of; positions cannot name them.

tree left
  1-1: /

tree right
  1-1: /
